{"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":181,"item_id":"msg_0f6f6c21e6e0b0f3016af03275c4b087d2b6ac3fb03515d648","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"If the absolute offset between instrument time and the observatory reference **exceeds two seconds**, the gateway must pause schedule execution, notify the duty operator, and leave queued reservations unchanged. It may resume only after **two consecutive reference checks** each report an offset within two seconds. [clock.md:3–7](clock.md#L3-L7)

If the reference clock is unavailable, execution must remain paused: a local clock reading alone cannot satisfy either recovery check. [clock.md:9–11](clock.md#L9-L11)

The gateway must not use the retired prototype’s recovery behavior of clearing pending reservations or restarting on the first local clock sample. A planner may compute a plan while execution is suspended, but that plan does not bypass the clock check or a weather interlock. [architecture.md:5–11](architecture.md#L5-L11)","logprobs":[]}

